In article <1993Mar18.185425.5058@nwnexus.wa.com> phaedrus@halcyon.com (Mark Phaedrus) writes:
>     I'm trying to compile NetHack 3.1 patchlevel 1 for the Macintosh, using
>the prepatched sources I just downloaded from linc.cis.upenn.edu.  I'm using
>stock System 7.1, no extensions, and a plain-vanilla installation of MPW
>3.2.3 (though 3.3b1 gave the same results).  The build works normally until
>it tries to use LevComp to process BigRoom.des, at which point it fails with
>a "read() in flex scanner failed" message.  Has anybody else run into this
>problem, and if so how did they get around it?

     Well, with the help of the NetHack team, I worked around this problem.
The LevComp and DgnComp files were compiled this time around with flex 
instead of lex, and while apparently other platforms like flex's code better,
the Mac doesn't like it at all.  Here's the workaround.  (Actually, this is
probably more than is necessary, but it works):
     1.  Find someplace where you can run lex and yacc (most Un*x boxes have
'em).
     2.  Copy all the "dgn_..." and "lev_..." files from your util directory
to that machine.
     3.  Run "yacc -d dgn_comp.y".  This will produce two files, y.tab.c and
y.tab.h, which you should rename to dgn_yacc.c and dgn_comp.h, respectively.
     4.  Run "yacc -d lev_comp.y", and rename the resulting files to 
lev_yacc.c and lev_comp.h.
     5.  Run "lex dgn_comp.l".  Rename the resulting C file to "dgn_lex.c".
     6.  Run "lex lev_comp.l".  Rename the resulting C file to "lev_lex.c".
     7.  Copy all six of these new files (dgn_yacc.c, dgn_comp.h, lev_yacc.c,
lev_comp.h, dgn_lex.c, lev_lex.c) to the sys:share directory on your Mac.
     8.  Do a full rebuild.  Contrary to Install.mpw, you shouldn't have to
alter the makefile; the dependencies for the .c files are already there, and
the .h files are automatically copied to the proper directory as part of the
build process.
     9.  Enjoy. :)
